{"id": "EUVD-2026-101131", "enisaUuid": "5c45eeb5-2a2e-3e55-8543-3766aed64d10", "description": "Sofia-SIP through 1.13.18 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in msg_multipart_parse() that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to crash the process by sending oversized MIME boundaries. Attackers can send an INVITE with a multipart Content-Type whose boundary exceeds the body length, causing memcmp to read past the heap buffer and crash the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T19:54:37", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/sofia-sip-multipart-oob-read", "https://github.com/freeswitch/sofia-sip/blob/ad36ac8f755308e8b87f98a505e83d4e408e5cc3/libsofia-sip-ua/msg/msg_mime.c#L404", "https://github.com/freeswitch/sofia-sip", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sofia-sip-through-1.13.18-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-msg-multipart-parse"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110658", "GHSA-9vj3-xq9j-5vq6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dd769937-d5c8-3eb0-89a9-65d29eaad686", "product": {"name": "sofia-sip", "vendor": {"name": "freeswitch"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.13.18"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e9451d5c-4b76-307e-b654-1b03472ed9fd", "vendor": {"name": "freeswitch"}}], "isExploited": false}